# Align with `docs/AGENTS.md`

For every code change in repo (new code, refactor, tests, wiring), follow `docs/AGENTS.md`.
Goal: keep product words, package boundaries, repo conventions aligned.

Before big edits, skim/re-read `docs/AGENTS.md` (and deeper refs it points to). Treat as source of truth for:

- Terminology: **guesschema** CLI, JSONL stdin → JSON Schema stdout, **`--read-window`**, library **`Guesser.Run`** (single emit).
- Layout/responsibility: **`cmd/guesschema`**, **`pkg/guesschema`**, **`internal/guesschema`** (implementation only, not tested directly); **`test/unit/pkg/guesschema`** = library contract; **`test/blackbox`** = CLI contract.
- Naming/imports: domain stays free of orchestration imports; **`internal` must not import `pkg`**; public API lives under **`pkg/`**.
- Errors: wrap with `%w` where appropriate; default slog discarded unless **`--debug`** (stderr).
- Anti-patterns: no catch-all `util` / `helpers`; **all tests under `test/` only** (no `*_test.go` in `cmd/`, `internal/`, `pkg/`); never import `internal/` from tests.

If generic advice conflicts with `docs/AGENTS.md`, pick `docs/AGENTS.md`.
If public behavior or big package boundaries change, update `docs/AGENTS.md` in same effort.
